Step 1: Open Browser

Open Google Chrome.

Step 2: Open Google Search Console

Go to:

Google Search Console

Step 3: Login with Gmail
Enter Gmail ID
Enter password
Login successfully
Step 4: Add Property (Website)
Click Add Property
Select:
URL Prefix

Example:

https://mywebsite.com
Click Continue
Step 5: Verify Website Ownership

Google asks verification.

Easy Method

Choose:

HTML File Upload OR
HTML Tag
For HTML Tag
Copy meta tag
Paste inside <head> section of website HTML

Example:

<meta name="google-site-verification" content="abc123">
Save file
Return to Search Console
Click Verify
Step 6: Create Sitemap

Create sitemap URL.

Example:

https://mywebsite.com/sitemap.xml
Step 7: Submit Sitemap
In left menu click Sitemaps
Enter:
sitemap.xml
Click Submit
Step 8: Request Indexing for a Page
Click URL Inspection
Enter website page URL

Example:

https://mywebsite.com/about.html
Click Enter
Click Request Indexing
Step 9: Wait for Google Processing

Google starts:

Crawling
Indexing
Showing page in search results

This may take few hours or days.

Step 10: Check Index Status
Open Search Console dashboard
View:
Indexed pages
Errors
Search performance
Step 11: Take Screenshots

Take screenshots of:

Search Console dashboard
Sitemap submission
URL inspection
Index request

(Useful for practical record)
